  "guideText": "1. Type or import TXT, DOCX, PDF or RTF.\n2. Choose a built-in font or upload a TTF font.\n3. Adjust paper, margins, spacing and variation. Upload a background and detect its margins if needed.\n4. Preview one or all pages, then export a PDF or image ZIP.\n\nThe backend applies a hand-drawn filter to illustrations. Use Prepare text to clean Markdown and convert formulas in one step. Choose handwritten or text table layouts. Blank lines and standalone page separators are removed, while code is preserved. Add page breaks and blank lines afterward if needed. Common symbols, fractions, roots, matrices and scripts are supported. Undo restores your original text. Paste a complete CircuiTikZ environment and generate a preview to draw common circuits with resistors, capacitors, inductors, sources and diodes. Unsupported diagrams retain their source.\n\nDrafts, illustrations and settings are stored on this device. Font and background files must be selected again. Backend tasks and results expire after about 30 minutes.",
